  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 104,
  "root_problem": "Since August 2026, billing dispute tickets have roughly doubled (590→1180→1260/month, E-07) primarily because the billing import/validation step of the meter-to-cash process is producing incorrect bills on accounts with ACTUAL meter reads (1,785 of 3,025 disputed bills) more often than on estimate-substituted bills (1,240) (E-01). This rules out slower ticket handling as the driver (response times stay within the 3.0-day SLA, E-02) and points away from read-collection failure as the dominant cause, leaving a defect in bill production from valid reads as the best-supported mechanism; a reported field-staffing shortfall (E-04/E-06) separately explains part of the smaller estimated-read-bill cohort."
 },
